  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Food Security and Boosting Farm Income for Women Smallholder Farmers in Rwanda-IFS Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The action is very relevant to the global objective of the call and, by promoting and supporting the production&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;of food and the eradication of malnutrition in Rwanda, it shares its vision of achieving a healthy, sustainable&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;and resilient food system. This action is also very pertinent to the priorities of the call since it targets the&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;empowerment of small-scale women farmers&#xbf; cooperatives with the necessary ecological farming skills and&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;collective capacities to access improved agri-inputs, and appropriately use innovative practices (including&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;agri-forestry, ecological irrigation and post-harvest handling technologies). It also strengthens existing local&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;selling and aggregation points. In doing this, it will help achieve a more socially and environmentally&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;inclusive agricultural value chains, contributing to increased food availability within the women producers&#xbf;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;households and the locally established markets.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
